#!/bin/sh
# Lance PR Radar et ouvre le navigateur.
set -e
cd "$(dirname "$0")"
PORT="${PORT:-4321}"
# /api/boot answers at once and only a PR Radar answers it, unlike / on a port taken by another app.
radar_up() { curl -sf "http://localhost:$PORT/api/boot" 2>/dev/null | grep -q '"boot"'; }
boot() { curl -sf "http://localhost:$PORT/api/boot" 2>/dev/null; }
browser_open() { boot | grep -q '"browsers":[1-9]'; }
if radar_up; then
  echo "PR Radar tourne déjà sur le port $PORT."
else
  node server.js &
  SERVER=$!
  until radar_up; do
    kill -0 "$SERVER" 2>/dev/null || exit 1
    sleep 0.3
  done
fi
FOUND=false
if boot | grep -q '"browsers"'; then
  # A tab left open reconnects to a fresh server within a second: give it the time before opening another.
  for TRY in 0 1 2 3 4 5 6; do
    [ "$TRY" -gt 0 ] && sleep 0.5
    if browser_open; then FOUND=true; break; fi
  done
else
  echo "Ce PR Radar ne sait pas repérer un onglet déjà ouvert : relance-le pour éviter un onglet en double."
fi
if $FOUND; then
  echo "Un onglet PR Radar est déjà ouvert : http://localhost:$PORT/"
else
  open "http://localhost:$PORT/"
fi
wait
